WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.506
Industrial communication hunts compare observed behavior with expected assets, roles, protocols, paths, timing, and operations.

00:00:07.506 --> 00:00:16.377
New devices or peers may represent replacement equipment, a vendor laptop, an inventory gap, or an unauthorized connection.

00:00:16.377 --> 00:00:20.244
Validate ownership and function before assigning intent.

00:00:20.244 --> 00:00:25.931
Unexpected protocol use can reveal a configuration change or unmanaged pathway.

00:00:25.931 --> 00:00:35.712
Protocol-aware telemetry may also show unusual read and write patterns, new engineering sessions, or operations inconsistent with the device role.

00:00:35.712 --> 00:00:41.853
The meaning depends on what the process was doing at the time.

00:00:41.853 --> 00:00:44.810
Controller-to-controller relationships are often stable.

00:00:44.810 --> 00:00:52.771
A new relationship, changed direction, or communication crossing an architectural zone can guide a focused hunt.

00:00:52.771 --> 00:00:59.368
Compare actual flows with approved conduits, firewall policy, network diagrams, and change records.

00:00:59.368 --> 00:01:00.960
Timing matters.

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:07.557
Activity outside production rhythm, maintenance windows, or normal polling intervals may deserve review.

00:01:07.557 --> 00:01:15.518
However, startup, failover, batch transitions, equipment faults, and communications recovery can also change volume and timing.

00:01:15.518 --> 00:01:18.930
Use passive data and existing records.

00:01:18.930 --> 00:01:26.891
Hunters should not generate writes, discovery traffic, or disruptive scans in production to test a theory.

00:01:26.891 --> 00:01:34.397
Correlate network evidence with controller status, historian trends, HMI alarms, remote sessions, and engineering activity.

00:01:34.397 --> 00:01:40.084
Document the baseline used, deviations found, operational explanation, and remaining uncertainty.

00:01:40.084 --> 00:01:44.861
A communication anomaly is a lead, not a verdict.

00:01:44.861 --> 00:01:54.187
The strongest finding links a meaningful change to asset identity, process context, supporting evidence, and a safe escalation path.
